.TH SHADERCANDY-BENCH 1 "2026-09-20" "ShaderCandy 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shadercandy-bench \- GPU shader performance benchmark
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shadercandy-bench
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shadercandy-bench
compiles all shaders, measures render FPS, and outputs a baseline performance
report. It uses an offscreen GLFW context for rendering and reports compile
times, average/min/max FPS per shader.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-dir " path"
Add a shader directory (can be used multiple times).
.TP
.BI \-frames " n"
Render frames per shader (default: 120).
.TP
.BI \-width " pixels"
Render width (default: 1920).
.TP
.BI \-height " pixels"
Render height (default: 1080).
.TP
.BI \-output " path"
Save report to a JSON file.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Show usage information.
.SH OUTPUT
The benchmark prints a table with columns: Shader name, compile time (ms),
average FPS, minimum FPS, and maximum FPS. A summary section follows with
aggregate statistics.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Benchmark all shaders in ./shaders
shadercandy-bench -dir shaders

# Benchmark with custom parameters
shadercandy-bench -dir shaders -frames 300 -width 1280 -height 720

# Save JSON report
shadercandy-bench -dir shaders -output baseline.json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shadercandy-screensaver (1),
.BR shadercandy-player (1)
.SH AUTHORS
ShaderCandy contributors.
